  "formulas": {
    "raw_nic_nodes_per_party": "ceil(G*QPS*words_per_output*field_bytes / (network_Gbps*1e9/8))",
    "headroom_nic_nodes_per_party": "ceil(raw_send_Bps*framing*hotspot / (NIC_Bps*nic_efficiency*capacity_utilization))",
    "conditional_cpu_nodes_per_party": "ceil(G*QPS*83 / (rate_per_64vCPU*(128/64)*capacity_utilization))",
    "annual_compute_usd": "nodes_per_party * parties * hourly_price * 8760",
    "all_cross_AZ_usd": "sum_over_parties(raw_send_Bps) * 31536000 / billing_unit_bytes * .02"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The network floor is conditional on a particular backend and its output count. It is not a universal MPC communication lower bound.",
    "G counts scalar reductions or dot-product OUTPUTS, not Boolean gates or dot-product scalar multiplications.",
    "The 83 weighted local operations is a scalar-reduction reference. Long dot products, random-bit production, exact conversion, sorting, checking, hashing and routing can add work independently.",
    "The CPU rates 0.5, 2 and 8 billion weighted operations per second per 64 vCPU are unmeasured assumptions; do not cite them as AWS or MPC performance.",
    "Node counts ignore storage capacity, state duplication, dependent-round latency, intraparty routing, imperfect distributed scaling, coordinator skew beyond the stated factor, setup, backups and failures.",
    "A raw NIC minimum need not be achievable. NIC efficiency and headroom factors are planning assumptions rather than guarantees.",
    "Cross-AZ transfer row uses raw protocol sends, without framing inflation; add it if budgeting wire overhead."
  ],
